{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability. The specifications encode a deterministic exploration policy that is safe under open-loop motion pulses: clear sensing drives random-walk exploration, a short forward pulse is allowed only from a dedicated progress state, and any obstacle event forces entry into a turn-recovery state before exploration resumes. Obstacle-side states use consistent directed turns, path_clear returns quickly to exploration, and full_rotate is reserved for a dedicated front-obstacle escape state rather than normal operation.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion in plant automata.",
    "Use small deterministic specifications to bind clear sensing to exploration actions and obstacle sensing to one-shot recovery turns.",
    "Alternate safe exploration between random_walk and short move_forward pulses to improve coverage without long forward streaks.",
    "Ensure every obstacle-triggered branch passes through a turn-recovery state and never enables move_forward or random_walk there."
  ],
